{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"9bd14a3422947fe534cbda3b7613bf735f2570b51564b1e3b0a8a62d33226fe0","occurred_at":"2026-11-23T06:34:21Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[388,390]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/triage_context_vectors.py","quoted_text":"    add(excerpt_case(\"excerpt-4300-digit-citation-is-past-the-end\", big, \"src/a.py:\" + \"9\" * 4300))\n    add(excerpt_case(\"excerpt-4301-digit-citation-is-a-value-error\", big, \"src/a.py:\" + \"9\" * 4301))\n    add(excerpt_case(\"excerpt-4301-digit-with-leading-zeros-is-a-value-error\", big, \"src/a.py:\" + \"0\" * 4300 + \"7\"))","reason":"The harness's 4300/4301-digit excerpt cases rely on Python's process-global int string-conversion cap (default 4300). If PYTHONINTMAXSTRDIGITS is lower, the 4300-digit citation raises ValueError instead of yielding the recorded past-the-end result, so --check reports a false stale fixture. Pinning sys.set_int_max_str_digits(4300) for run_context with restoration is the minimal compatible fix; no contract clause overrides this ordinary test-stability defect.","target":"199a4d9d782b18a4e267cd7298517741ef168249"},"finding_id":"4208e2b3ea3209636dde9bb137b2ee6c20d6abe0d20476929d89cbeedd9ae838","previous_event_id":null,"review_id":"b40363202a5f67d88bb455adc4ad0098d84e7dbd74db7025955f4242f6ecbdeb"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:4208e2b3ea3209636dde9bb137b2ee6c20d6abe0d20476929d89cbeedd9ae838:99439925d1a9794ff35f6e199c425038d85983721b61b83dd146df028d19cc4f"}